WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
The Warlords of the Sea are one of the strongest&nbsp;
groups of pirates in One Piece. Some of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.900
are nearly as powerful as the Emperors and&nbsp;
some simply have ridiculously over-powered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.380
devil fruits. Yet none of them has ever&nbsp;
gone on to become king of the pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.380
so far at least. But what would happen if Luffy&nbsp;
had eaten their crazy devil fruits instead?

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.240
And even though it would obviously be a ton of fun&nbsp;
to think about Luffy having Mihawk’s sword skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.260
since we’re talking about devil fruits&nbsp;
specifically for this video the focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:33.900
will be on Crocodile’s absurdly powerful Sand&nbsp;
fruit, Gecko Moria’s sinister Shadow fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.480
Doflamingo’s manipulative String fruit, and&nbsp;
Bartholemew Kuma’s unbelievably overpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.680
Paw fruit. The pirate Empress Boa Hancock&nbsp;
was also one of the original warlords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.780
but her fruit makes absolutely no sense for&nbsp;
Luffy, so we aren’t going to include it.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:56.460
So we begin in Luffy’s childhood, where kid Luffy&nbsp;
is eying not one but five treasure boxes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.740
Shanks’ crew has left lying around the bar. One&nbsp;
of these contains Luffy’s original devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.800
and the others have the Warlord’s devil fruits&nbsp;
that we’ll assume that somehow Shanks stole. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.620
the always hungry Luffy sneakily steals a treasure&nbsp;
chest and takes a bite of this weird looking fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:19.440
inside. And as he’s munching away, Shanks and&nbsp;
the crew go absolutely bonkers. Shanks grabs his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:26.520
arm and instantly a little shadow clone of Luffy&nbsp;
comes up from the floor to slap away Shanks’ hand.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.800
May I now introduce, Shadow Luffy.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.660
And before we get into all of the surprisingly&nbsp;
crazy changes this would have on the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.340
let’s talk for a second about devil fruits&nbsp;
and personalities. In a previous video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.620
I explained how there is a pretty strong theory&nbsp;
that devil fruits contain a will of their own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.800
and when someone eats a devil fruit then the&nbsp;
fruit’s will can affect the person who ate it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:55.680
For example, Gecko Moria, the original user of&nbsp;
the Shadow fruit, is pretty damn lazy and uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.440
other people’s shadows to do his dirty work.&nbsp;
But was this Moria just utilizing his fruit or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.780
was the nature of the shadow fruit encouraging&nbsp;
him to use the powers in this way? Similarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:12.840
Doflamingo’s string fruit can literally make&nbsp;
people into puppets, so was it just the perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:18.240
fruit for Doflamingo or did the fruit encourage&nbsp;
him to become an evil, underground puppet master?

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.040
And we even see a bit of this with&nbsp;
Luffy during his fight with Kaido,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.260
where Luffy is laughing uncontrollably after&nbsp;
awakening his original devil fruit powers.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:34.320
So because Luffy is eating a different devil&nbsp;
fruit, his personality may change slightly. He may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.900
not be the guy who ALWAYS bounces back from defeat&nbsp;
because that was the main characteristic of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.640
original devil fruit. And someone like Ace would&nbsp;
probably get his original devil fruit instead.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:53.760
And with that in mind, let’s dive right into&nbsp;
the shady powers of the Shadow Fruit. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.100
this fruit allows you to manipulate shadows,&nbsp;
both your own and other people’s. On the zombie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.120
island Thriller Bark, we learned that Moria&nbsp;
can take shadows from other people and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:10.920
use them to bring corpses back to life or to&nbsp;
massively increase his own strength. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.580
his own shadow basically became&nbsp;
a second version of himself that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.320
can act independently. So this is&nbsp;
a seriously powerful devil fruit.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:28.740
However for Luffy, this fruit is THE ABSOLUTE&nbsp;
WORST match out of these four warlord fruits. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:35.460
other fruit fit his personality way better, as we&nbsp;
will see later in the video, but this one is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:41.880
to present major obstacles for Luffy. And that’s&nbsp;
because the downside of taking someone’s shadow is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:48.480
that they will die if they go in sunlight. So this&nbsp;
leaves us with two options. First is that Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:54.480
doesn’t ever take someone else’s shadow, meaning&nbsp;
he doesn’t use the fruit’s main power. Or second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.720
is that his personality is completely changed&nbsp;
by the devil fruit. In this case, Shadow Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.420
would no longer care about other people dying, so&nbsp;
he is totally fine stealing shadows from anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:13.500
he meets. But while this didn’t bother Moria, I&nbsp;
simply cannot imagine Luffy taking shadows from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:18.060
innocent people and then just leaving them to&nbsp;
die or hide in the dark the rest of their lives.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.960
So if he isn’t going to steal shadows,&nbsp;
that basically leaves Luffy with just his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.120
own shadow to manipulate. Which is still&nbsp;
pretty badass because it is basically an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:37.200
unkillable copy of yourself. So let’s see&nbsp;
how far Luffy can go with these powers.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.540
After training for ten years, I think Luffy&nbsp;
would definitely learn how to use his shadow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:48.240
clone incredibly well. He could make it appear,&nbsp;
block attacks, fight for him, and even seamlessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.520
swap places with his shadow. So while I don’t&nbsp;
think he would have any problem in the East Blue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.980
the real challenge comes in Alabasta against&nbsp;
the Warlord Crocodile. As we already mentioned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:04.860
Crocodile has the sand devil fruit which turns&nbsp;
his body into sand. And just like any Logia this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:11.820
means that he is virtually untouchable unless&nbsp;
someone uses haki or discovers their elemental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:16.680
weakness. And in the original story, Luffy&nbsp;
was only able to defeat him by getting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:22.920
sand wet with blood and water. And even then&nbsp;
Luffy suffered two crushing defeats twice and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:28.800
only lived because of a combination of&nbsp;
luck, his allies, and his rubbed body.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.000
However, Shadow Luffy would&nbsp;
have none of these advantages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:39.060
and would even be much less skilled at combat.&nbsp;
Luffy’s body is normal and cannot stretch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:44.820
so he is basically just a normal fighter with&nbsp;
his shadow clone. But since he cannot use haki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:50.040
yet and his body wouldn’t be as durable, I do&nbsp;
not think Luffy would survive this encounter.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:57.780
But even if he did survive, he would definitely&nbsp;
lose to another strong fighter in the Grand Line.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:06.000
So goodbye Shadow Luffy.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.440
And if this version of Luffy could not even&nbsp;
make it past the first half of the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:14.700
will any of these new devil fruits&nbsp;
be strong enough for Luffy to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:21.240
pirate king? Some of these upcoming&nbsp;
storylines are absolutely insane.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.200
Because while the Shadow fruit&nbsp;
was a truly awful match for Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.880
this next one will allow him&nbsp;
to unleash his full power.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:36.540
So Reset. Back to chapter 1. Only this&nbsp;
time hungry kid Luffy eats this devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:42.180
fruit. Shanks grabs his arm, and instantly a&nbsp;
razor-sharp string pops out and cuts Shanks’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.100
hand. Looks like this time in the devil&nbsp;
fruit lottery, Luffy won the string fruit.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.640
And originally this fruit was&nbsp;
eaten by Donquixote Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:57.360
the Warlord who conquered the kingdom of&nbsp;
Alabasta. This fruit allows you to produce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.520
and control an infinite amount of string&nbsp;
which can be used to make life-like clones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:08.280
attach his string to other people to make them his&nbsp;
puppets, and even stitch together internal wounds.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:15.480
So this fruit is super versatile and is a perfect&nbsp;
fit for Luffy’s creativity. So he will surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:20.460
take advantage of the ten years training&nbsp;
to become an expert at using his strings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:25.320
But since Doffy was a cold-hearted monster,&nbsp;
we have to wonder if the fruit would make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:31.800
Luffy become more manipulative as well. Would&nbsp;
Luffy still gather such a loyal crew? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:43.560
I think so because even Doflamingo was fiercely&nbsp;
loyal to his core crew. But he was totally fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:48.600
using other people. And while I don’t think Luffy&nbsp;
will follow completely in Doflamingo’s footsteps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:53.100
there are plenty of ways for him to use the&nbsp;
strings without controlling innocent people.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:02.280
And compared to Luffy’s base rubber form,&nbsp;
String Luffy is arguably much stronger. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:08.460
can fly like spider man, fire string bullets,&nbsp;
and even cut with his sharp string. So I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:13.140
Luffy would have an even easier time in&nbsp;
the East Blue than in the original story.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:21.480
But moving ahead to the first major challenge,&nbsp;
Crocodile. Luffy would again have a harder time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:26.940
discovering the secret of Logia fruit weaknesses.&nbsp;
Since most of String Luffy’s attacks come from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:32.040
distance, he will have a harder time learning that&nbsp;
his blood or water can allow him to actually hurt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:37.560
the Sand fruit user. But because Luffy can fly&nbsp;
around and he doesn’t have to physically punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.780
he would probably survive longer during the&nbsp;
fight, and eventually learn the secret to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:49.140
Crocodile. Or maybe he traps Crocodile in a super&nbsp;
compact ball of string and dumps him in the ocean.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.800
However, the lightning fruit user Enel is&nbsp;
on a completely different level. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:00.840
Luffy does not have his natural rubber&nbsp;
immunity, and he doesn’t yet have haki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:07.260
the Lightning fruit user would probably destroy&nbsp;
Luffy. However, it is also possible that String&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:13.260
Luffy is so smart at using his devil fruit that he&nbsp;
could make giant string conductors to channel the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:19.380
lightning away from himself. He still wouldn’t&nbsp;
be able to hit Enel, unless he uses Sea Stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:24.720
so either way this is going to be very difficult&nbsp;
and probably lead to Luffy’s defeat. On the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:30.120
hand, maybe String Luffy is smarter about&nbsp;
escaping and simply runs away to survive.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:39.000
But let’s assume he did win, or he just escaped.&nbsp;
Then he would still probably need to be saved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:45.480
after losing to Aokiji. But then Water 7 and Enies&nbsp;
Lobby would be a breeze. Since he can fly around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:51.060
I think he has a much easier time saving Robin&nbsp;
and defeating CP9. Because one of the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.800
advantages of this fruit is that he can attack&nbsp;
from a distance, so he doesn’t need to even be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:02.460
close to deal insane amounts of damage to this&nbsp;
leopard man. And even if Robin did get captured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:10.920
Luffy could make his own version of the birdcage&nbsp;
to make sure she wasn’t taken away. Plus Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:16.620
could also make keys out of string to unlock&nbsp;
her handcuffs, making her rescue much simpler.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.440
And Moria would be a joke to fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:24.360
especially because Luffy can even&nbsp;
control the shadow zombies like puppets.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:27.000
And I don’t see any real&nbsp;
changes to Sabaody either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:32.280
but Impel down would be completely different.&nbsp;
Luffy would still need help sneaking in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:38.280
but then Luffy can travel between levels super&nbsp;
easily. He could also slice open prison bars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.960
so it is highly likely that he could save his&nbsp;
brother before Ace is taken to Marineford.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:48.840
Luffy’s fight with this venomous warden&nbsp;
would also be WAY easier. Attacking from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:54.180
a distance means that Luffy can easily avoid&nbsp;
the warden’s deadly poisons and I think he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:59.760
has a strong chance of winning this fight.&nbsp;
Similarly, in his encounter with Blackbeard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.620
Luffy could slash the darkness man before&nbsp;
he has a chance to enact his evil plan.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:11.580
But let’s say that maybe Luffy got caught in a&nbsp;
cloud of poison gas and Ace was still taken to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.200
Marineford. Now although Luffy might be able to&nbsp;
get to Ace more easily during this epic battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:21.000
I still think he would be overwhelmed by the&nbsp;
monstrously strong fighters on the battlefield.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:27.300
So this leads us to the time skip and once Luffy&nbsp;
learns Haki EVERYTHING CHANGES. After training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:33.540
for two years, Luffy is now a master with his&nbsp;
haki-coated strings and can take on anyone.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:40.080
The fishman Hoady and the evil scientist Caesar&nbsp;
would be no problem. There would be no conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:44.640
in Dressrosa since Doflamingo doesn’t have his&nbsp;
string fruit and never took over the country.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:51.600
Of course, Big Mom and Kaido would still be&nbsp;
major obstacles, but these clashes are more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:56.520
about superior haki than devil fruit powers,&nbsp;
so I think Luffy would still come out on top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:02.220
just like in the main story, leaving Luffy&nbsp;
well on his way to becoming pirate king.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:05.040
So with one devil fruit turning out very very bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.820
and one working perfectly for&nbsp;
Luffy to continue on his journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:14.700
what will happen to Luffy’s journey when he gets&nbsp;
the two most powerful devil fruits on this list?

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:20.220
Now let’s cycle back to chapter one again,&nbsp;
where Luffy has stolen this devil fruit and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:26.040
takes a giant bite. Alarmed, Shanks grabs&nbsp;
Luffy’s arm and POOF, it explodes into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:32.280
cloud of sand. Shanks jaw drops, and&nbsp;
Luffy dissolves into a pile of sand.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:39.120
But now armed with the same fruit that defeated&nbsp;
Shadow Luffy, let’s see how far Sand Luffy can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.400
go. And it might actually surprise with some&nbsp;
of the new challenges he has to overcome

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.960
And since this is a Logia fruit which&nbsp;
turns Luffy’s entire body into sand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:53.700
it is arguably the strongest of the four devil&nbsp;
fruits in this video. Just like any other Logia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.860
he cannot be hit by anyone who doesn’t know&nbsp;
haki. He can transform into a cloud of sand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:04.560
dry things out with touch, and create&nbsp;
sharp blades of sand to attack opponents.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:09.660
However, as we discussed earlier all Logia’s&nbsp;
have some elemental weakness and this fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:15.480
has the biggest one in the whole story.&nbsp;
Water. If Sand Luffy gets wet from water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:21.240
or blood or some other liquid, he immediately&nbsp;
loses his invincibility. And unfortunately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:27.180
for Sand Luffy, water just happens to&nbsp;
be literally everywhere in this world.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:33.780
But East Blue would still be a breeze, except&nbsp;
maybe if this fishman was constantly wet. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:38.640
is a debate about Sand Luffy versus the Smoke&nbsp;
Logia fruit user, Smoker, but with his body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:44.040
being literally sand Luffy wouldn’t have even&nbsp;
been captured in Logue Town in the first place.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.780
And even if Crocodile somehow managed to take&nbsp;
over Alabasta without his sand powers, this desert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.780 --> 00:14:01.020
kingdom is literally the best place for Luffy to&nbsp;
fight, so Luffy would defeat Crocodile easily.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:06.360
But the bigger question is how will Sand&nbsp;
Luffy do against other overpowered Logia’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:10.560
like Enel and the marine admirals?&nbsp;
And this becomes highly dependent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:14.640
on matchups. So let’s analyze&nbsp;
these fights for just a minute.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:18.840
Against Enel, Sand is actually a&nbsp;
very poor conductor of electricity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:23.700
so while Luffy may not be completely unaffected&nbsp;
by lightning like he was with his rubber body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:30.120
he would still have a strong chance since&nbsp;
all lightning would do is heat up the sand.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:36.240
But while Luffy might do well in Skypiea, once he&nbsp;
comes down to the sea, he would face his ABSOLUTE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:41.640
WORST matchup in the story against the Ice&nbsp;
Logia user Aokiji. Since Aokiji would have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:48.960
near constant source of melting ice and he knows&nbsp;
haki there is ZERO CHANCE Luffy would win this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:56.340
fight. And Aokiji would demand Luffy subscribe to&nbsp;
the channel for more of these What ifs… or else.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:15:00.120
And then the story progresses pretty&nbsp;
much the same through the time skip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:06.900
when Luffy would learn haki. This makes the&nbsp;
post-time skip even easier since he can now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:13.560
pretty easily fight other Logia users. But ALL&nbsp;
THIS CHANGES when we reach the most fearsome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:18.480
opponents: Big Mom and Kaido. And as we’ve&nbsp;
already discussed, these battles are intense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:26.460
clashes of supreme haki. And surely, most&nbsp;
definitely, Sand Luffy would stand NO CHANCE.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:30.540
And before you go crazy in the comments,&nbsp;
let me explain. In chapter 886,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:36.000
we are told in a flashback that haki&nbsp;
blooms most during intense battle. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.320
since Sand Luffy’s logia powers gave him a&nbsp;
much easier time during the post time skip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:47.520
he hasn’t had to endure the same struggles which&nbsp;
allowed him to truly master haki. And this comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:52.560
back to bite him later on, as Kaido&nbsp;
and Big Mom would absolutely destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:56.760
him and his underdeveloped haki,&nbsp;
bringing an end to Sand Luffy.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:02.520
So with three fruits down and one&nbsp;
to go, this brings us to the final,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:11.220
and most life-changing fruit in this video.&nbsp;
Back in the bar, Luffy takes a bite of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:16.980
mysterious fruit. Shanks loses his mind and grabs&nbsp;
him, staring at the strange paw pads on Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:23.940
hands. But then Luffy freaks out and a huge&nbsp;
explosion of air demolishes the entire building.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:24.480
Whoops.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:30.540
And this begins the most interesting&nbsp;
part of this What If scenario. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:35.640
the Paw fruit was one of my Top 5 most&nbsp;
overpowered devil fruits in a recent video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:42.480
and its powers are truly mind-blogging. It was&nbsp;
used by the former Warlord Bartholemew Kuma and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:48.060
its powers allow you to repel anything. This means&nbsp;
that any kind of attack can be easily blocked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:53.160
But even crazier is that you can repel&nbsp;
things like air to make a compression bomb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.960
or you can push yourself so fast that you&nbsp;
can literally travel across the world.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:02.700
But the most insane part of this&nbsp;
fruit is that it can even repel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:06.960
intangible concepts like pain or&nbsp;
memories from a person’s body.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:13.260
Now can you imagine Luffy learning to&nbsp;
control this fruit and all the wild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:20.640
imaginative things that he could do with it? The&nbsp;
potential for Luffy and this fruit are limitless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:26.760
Could he push pain out of himself to heal?&nbsp;
Could he push hunger out of himself to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:32.400
it so that he is never hungry? Or how about&nbsp;
his stupidity? Could that make him smarter?

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:38.400
And after ten years of training, Luffy&nbsp;
wouldn’t even need a ship. He can simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:44.340
push himself across the sea to wherever he wants&nbsp;
to go. And while I don’t think Luffy will be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:49.200
master of this just yet, because he probably&nbsp;
wouldn’t know the world’s geography too well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:54.240
he should be able to do small pushes to&nbsp;
keep him in the air and go between islands.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:59.820
But one of the most interesting questions&nbsp;
with this fruit is would Paw Luffy even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:04.620
gather a crew? For example, while Kuma was&nbsp;
a founding member of the Revolutionary army,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:11.340
we almost always see him by himself. Was&nbsp;
this just Kuma’s personality or was it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:16.140
something about the fruit that naturally&nbsp;
repelled other people? And if we apply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:21.120
that same idea to Luffy, would this fruit&nbsp;
make him less willing to gather a crew?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:25.620
But for now, let’s assume that Paw Luffy&nbsp;
still meets Zoro and Nami. But things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:31.140
completely change once they steal the map&nbsp;
of the grand line from this clown. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:37.980
Paw Luffy is super excited about the Grand&nbsp;
Line. And before Nami can talk him out of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:42.960
Luffy launches the three of them straight&nbsp;
to the entrance to the Grand Line, Reverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:46.980
Mountain. But as they’re hanging in the air,&nbsp;
Nami is shouting at Luffy, demanding that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:52.920
take them back. Meanwhile, Luffy and Zoro argue&nbsp;
about which direction to take. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:57.060
knowing these two, instead of entering the&nbsp;
much safer starting point of the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:03.720
they take a completely wrong turn and end up near&nbsp;
the end of the Grand Line, at Egghead Island.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:08.940
And this wrong turn nearly spells the end&nbsp;
of this massively unprepared crew. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:13.440
they land at the secret laboratory of the&nbsp;
genius scientist Dr. Vegapunk. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:20.040
Vegapunk is incredibly interested in Paw Luffy’s&nbsp;
powers. Because we recently learned that Kuma used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:26.520
the fruit to aid Vegapunk’s research. But Luffy&nbsp;
has no interest in staying to do some science,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:31.380
so he launches the group across the&nbsp;
sea straight onto this evil looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:36.780
skull dome. And this, of course, is the&nbsp;
home of the Emperor of the Sea, Kaido.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:43.620
And it’s at this point, Nami is seriously&nbsp;
regretting ever joining Paw Luffy. But while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:48.840
sneaking around the island, they meet Yamato, the&nbsp;
child or Kaido, who has been trapped on the island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:54.240
by her father. And of course Yamato knows exactly&nbsp;
who Luffy is, since they met with Ace a few years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:59.820
ago, and they are desperate to go out to sea&nbsp;
with the trio. So Luffy uses his Paw powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:07.560
to push off their handcuffs just as Kaido finds&nbsp;
them. And he is furious that these random pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:14.100
have invaded his castle. He charges up a full&nbsp;
dragon blast breath. Nami is screaming with fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:19.980
but Luffy grabs them all and pushes them out&nbsp;
to safety, all the way back to the East Blue.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:29.700
And after landing, the crew is exhausted. But&nbsp;
Luffy and Yamato think it was all hilarious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:36.240
while Nami is furious and Zoro just wants some&nbsp;
booze. But it’s at this point that Nami beats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:40.980
into Luffy’s head that they can’t just skip&nbsp;
ahead because there are people way too powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:46.980
for them. So Luffy decides to actually do things&nbsp;
right, and build a proper crew with a real ship.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.520
And with Yamato along for the ride,&nbsp;
this changes everything since they is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:55.500
nearly as strong as Kaido already. So the&nbsp;
East Blue is pathetically easy for them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.900
and they enter the Grand Line full of confidence.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:05.040
But Yamato is not just a strong fighter.&nbsp;
They also know all about haki, so they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:11.040
able to teach the crew the basics. And this&nbsp;
allows the crew to easily take out Crocodile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:15.780
Enel, and even give Aokiji a difficult fight.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:23.400
And since this version of Luffy uses the Paw&nbsp;
fruit instead of Kuma, this means the crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:27.780
would not be separated at Sabaody. They&nbsp;
would still need to escape from Kizaru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:31.920
but with Rayleigh’s help I think they&nbsp;
would be able to all get away together.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:39.300
And this brings us to Marineford, where the buffed&nbsp;
up version of the crew comes ever so close to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:47.580
saving Ace. But the combined force of the marines&nbsp;
is just too much, and Ace eventually is killed.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:52.500
Which brings us to the time-skip. Now&nbsp;
it’s possible the crew could go on ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:57.780
to Fishman Island right away since they are&nbsp;
all together, but I think the crushing defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:03.300
would mean they still decide to wait and train&nbsp;
for a bit before heading into the New World.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:06.360
But when they do enter the&nbsp;
New World after the time skip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:12.480
they have even more motivation to take down&nbsp;
Kaido because Yamato would definitely tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:16.500
them all about the situation on Wano.&nbsp;
She might even recognize these two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:20.460
samurai right away and the Straw Hats would&nbsp;
definitely want to help save their country.

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:24.960
And the crew would pretty&nbsp;
easily move through Dressrosa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:30.720
which brings us to the Emperor’s saga. And&nbsp;
this part of Paw Luffy’s story is incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:35.460
difficult to speculate about because the&nbsp;
most important part of fighting the Yonko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:41.340
is having ridiculously strong haki. But we&nbsp;
don’t exactly know how haki interacts with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:46.800
Luffy’s devil fruit. So unless Luffy becomes&nbsp;
an absolute powerhouse with his devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:51.780
he might struggle with some of the strongest&nbsp;
fighters like Kaido and Big Mom. Or he might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:56.880
just have to learn to fight with his bare hands&nbsp;
and feet in order to really use his haki powers.

00:22:56.880 --> 00:23:03.960
On the other hand, the limits of this fruit&nbsp;
are still unknown. Luffy could become the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:09.420
overpowered devil fruit user and simply defeat&nbsp;
everyone with his Paw fruit. For example, could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:15.420
he push the soul out of big mom’s homies? Or could&nbsp;
he push a devil fruit power out of someone like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:22.680
Kaido, making him lose all of his dragon powers?&nbsp;
Seriously, this fruit is wild and until we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:28.500
more about it, it is hard to say how Luffy would&nbsp;
fare against the strongest fighters in the story.

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:33.900
But the biggest question for all of these devil&nbsp;
fruits is if Luffy would still become the pirate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:39.660
king. Shadow Luffy would definitely fail,&nbsp;
and I think Sand Luffy would as well. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:46.200
String Luffy and Paw Luffy definitely have&nbsp;
a chance to pursue the ultimate dream. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:51.900
one thing that will be the same no matter what&nbsp;
fruit Luffy has, are Luffy’s rivals. Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:56.160
and Shanks are the ultimate powers standing&nbsp;
in his way, and if you want to see what would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:03.000
happen if Luffy fought Blackbeard and Shanks&nbsp;
for the One Piece, you can click right here.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.380
Shanks for watching.

